-- title:
--   Rational homomorphisms separate ℓ-torsion under quaternionic endomorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$, and let $X_0$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ that is elliptic. Fix $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$ of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of the predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Assume given an injective ring homomorphism $\theta$ from [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring κ X₀`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32) — the subring of the additive endomorphism ring of the group of points of $X_0$ base changed to $\kappa$ generated by those endomorphisms that are either zero or given, outside a finite exceptional set of $x$-coordinates, by a fixed quadruple of bivariate polynomials over $\kappa$ as $(n_X/d_X, n_Y/d_Y)$ with non-vanishing denominators — into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, whose range is exactly $\Lambda$. Let $W$ be a further elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ and $\chi$ a nonzero additive homomorphism from the points of $X_0$ to the points of $W$ lying in `rationalHomSet`, i.e. zero or rationally represented in the above sense. Let $\ell$ be a prime different from $q'$ and $Q$ a nonzero point of $W$ with $\ell\cdot Q=0$. Then there is a $\rho$ in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet κ W X₀`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28) with $\rho(Q)\neq 0$.
--
--   This is the level-$\ell$ form of the Deuring–Tate description of homomorphisms between supersingular elliptic curves: rational homomorphisms from $W$ to $X_0$ suffice to separate the points of order $\ell$ on $W$, for $\ell$ different from the characteristic. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where kernels of rational homomorphisms between curves with quaternionic endomorphism rings are matched with ideals of the order $\Lambda$.
-- source:
